{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"51544ebab7ff7963","name":"card_event_usaaf","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/OceaniaStorm/events/card_event_usaaf","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"USAAF","text":"Draw a US bomber and a US fighter from your deck.","flavorText":"The United States Army Air Forces, or USAAF, was created in June 1941 as the main land-based air arm of the U.S. Army. It rapidly expanded from the much smaller pre-war Air Corps into one of the largest military organizations of WWII, reaching more than 2.4 million personnel and nearly 80,000 aircraft at its peak in 1944. The USAAF fought across every major theater of the war. In Europe, the Eighth and Fifteenth Air Forces carried out the strategic bombing campaign against German industry, transportation and oil production, while tactical air forces supported Allied ground troops. In the Pacific, USAAF units operated from New Guinea, China and island bases across the Central Pacific. During the final stage of the war, the Twentieth Air Force used long-range B-29 Superfortress bombers to strike the Japanese home islands. By the end of WWII, the USAAF had effectively become an independent air service in all but name. Its wartime experience led to the creation of the independent United States Air Force in September 1947.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_usaaf","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_usaaf_title","SourceString":"USAAF","LocalizedString":"USAAF"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_usaaf_text","SourceString":"Draw a US bomber and a US fighter from your deck.","LocalizedString":"Draw a US bomber and a US fighter from your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_usaaf_history","SourceString":"The United States Army Air Forces, or USAAF, was created in June 1941 as the main land-based air arm of the U.S. Army. It rapidly expanded from the much smaller pre-war Air Corps into one of the largest military organizations of WWII, reaching more than 2.4 million personnel and nearly 80,000 aircraft at its peak in 1944. The USAAF fought across every major theater of the war. In Europe, the Eighth and Fifteenth Air Forces carried out the strategic bombing campaign against German industry, transportation and oil production, while tactical air forces supported Allied ground troops. In the Pacific, USAAF units operated from New Guinea, China and island bases across the Central Pacific. During the final stage of the war, the Twentieth Air Force used long-range B-29 Superfortress bombers to strike the Japanese home islands. By the end of WWII, the USAAF had effectively become an independent air service in all but name. Its wartime experience led to the creation of the independent United States Air Force in September 1947.","LocalizedString":"The United States Army Air Forces, or USAAF, was created in June 1941 as the main land-based air arm of the U.S. Army. It rapidly expanded from the much smaller pre-war Air Corps into one of the largest military organizations of WWII, reaching more than 2.4 million personnel and nearly 80,000 aircraft at its peak in 1944. The USAAF fought across every major theater of the war. In Europe, the Eighth and Fifteenth Air Forces carried out the strategic bombing campaign against German industry, transportation and oil production, while tactical air forces supported Allied ground troops. In the Pacific, USAAF units operated from New Guinea, China and island bases across the Central Pacific. During the final stage of the war, the Twentieth Air Force used long-range B-29 Superfortress bombers to strike the Japanese home islands. By the end of WWII, the USAAF had effectively become an independent air service in all but name. Its wartime experience led to the creation of the independent United States Air Force in September 1947."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/USAAF.USAAF","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_usaaf_photo","SourceString":"A formation of USAAF P-51 Mustang fighters over Saipan, Northern Mariana Islands, 1945.","LocalizedString":"A formation of USAAF P-51 Mustang fighters over Saipan, Northern Mariana Islands, 1945."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"isAttackBuff":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"BomberCardid","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"fighterCardid","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"cardToDraw","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_usaaf","owner":"card_event_usaaf_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetAllCards_cards","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Get_Item","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Length_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsBomber_isIt","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Less_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsFighter_isIt","type":"bool","direc